 "title": "Welcome to Osage County,MO",
 "text": "Welcome to Osage County,MO\nGO\nSearch\nHome\nCounty Offices\n911/Emergency Management\nCircuit Clerk\nCounty Clerk\nCollector of Revenue\nCounty Assessor\nCounty Commission\nCounty Coroner\nCounty Health Department\nCounty Recorder\nCounty Sheriff\nCounty Surveyor\nCounty Treasurer\nProsecuting Attorney\nPublic Administrator\nRoad and Bridge Department\nUniversity of Missouri Extension\nResidents\nChurches\nLibrary\nParks & Recreation\nCounty Schools\nTowns in Osage County\nVoter Registration\nWeather\nCemetery Information\nVisitors\nAccommodations\nDining\nOsage County Historical Society\nUpcoming Events\nVisit Osage County\nCounty Resources\nAmeren Missouri\nLicense DMV\nMissouri Association of Counties (MAC)\nMissouri Court Case\nMissouri Ethics Commission\nMissouri Revised Statutes\nMO Attorney General\nMO Dept. of Natural Resources (DNR)\nMO Secretary of State\nMO State Highway Patrol (MSHP)\nPay Taxes Online\nState Historic Preservation Office (SHPO)\nSunshine Law Request Form\nThree Rivers Electric\nHow Do I\nContact Us\nPay Taxes Online\nCommission Meeting Minutes & Agenda\nView a Map of Osage County\nOSAGE COUNTY\nCOVID-19 COMMUNICATION\nCOVID-19 Transition to Endemic Guidelines\nOnline Bill Pay\nLearn More\nElection Results\nLearn More\nMeeting Minutes\nLearn More\nEmployee Information\nLearn More\nExplore\nOur County\nLIVE\nWORK\nPLAY\nNews &\nAnnouncements\nMay 09, 2025\nBank Bids\nNov 19, 2024\nView/Print Tax Receipts\nSep 01, 2023\nSpeed Limit on County Roads\nView All News\nAbout Us\nOsage County is a county located in the central portion of the U.S. state of Missouri . Its county seat is Linn, also known as the “mile long city”. The county, originally part of Gasconade County, was organized January 29, 1841 by Hon. A. Alexander of Gasconade County when he proposed the act which was passed and approved creating Osage County. The name was derived from the French, “Oua Chage”, and through the practice of spelling names as they sounded resulted in Osage. The territory now Osage County was the hunting ground of the Delaware, Shawnee and a large, strong tribe, of Osage Indians. The Indians were not only good hunters, they raised quantities of Indian corn. Most of their activities were confined to the rivers and streams and they were of a peaceful nature.\nNow, Osage County Seat in Linn consists of two buildings. The Courthouse located at 106 E. Main Street with the offices of the Sheriff/Jail, Prosecuting Attorney and the Circuit Clerk currently reside.\nThe Osage County Administration Building also known as the Annex Building is located at 205 E. Main Street with the offices of 911/Emergency Management on the lower lever, Health Department, Assessor, Collector, and Recorder on the main floor and the Treasurer, County Clerk, Commission and University of Missouri Extension located on the second floor.\n© 2017 Osage County,MO\n205 E. Main Street, Linn, MO 65051\nPowered By\nRevize\nLogin\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and past this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://osagecountygov.com/\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose",
